 "notes": "Flood depth indicator, no border, black on white; three variants (G9-22-1 m 2/1, G9-22-2 m 4/3, G9-22-3 m 6/5) are drawn on the one PNG G9-22-1.png. Marks every 200 (0.2 m): 350 from the top to the first mark, 200 to the bottom below the last (0.2-step numeral baseline). Numeral baselines on the marks: whole metres 160 D centred with a 25 x 20 tick at each edge; intermediate values 60 D at the construction line x=37 (lines at 37/75/112/150 from the left) with a 50 x 20 tick at x 150-200. Tick 20 thick placed with its bottom on the mark (tick/baseline relation read from the drawing, not stated). m 125 Emod centred, baseline 140 (the 140 dimension); the 125 Emod bracket is drawn from the top edge but the chain 140+50+160 = 350 puts the cap top at 15 (15 mm drawing inconsistency). The \"25 | 140\" callout at the top right and the 37/38 construction lines are ambiguous - tick lengths taken as 25 (whole metre) and 50 (0.2 step). Spec written from G9-22-1.png (no separate PNG)."
